(Critical: write down everything they mention as you go. You’ll recap it in a moment.)

First, have you noticed any more shifting or crowding since we last spoke? Teeth are like books on a shelf, once they start to lean, they keep leaning, and most people notice it in photos before they notice it in the mirror.

{{pt_floss_q}}

{{pt_bite_q}}

{{pt_jaw_q}} A bite that’s off has a sneaky way of showing up everywhere but the teeth.

{{pt_al_photos_q}}

Finally, any changes in dental health since we last saw {{pt_them}}? New dental work, gum concerns, anything the dentist has flagged?

(Recap what you wrote down, including the shifting they mentioned at the start, then ask:)

Now {{contact_first_name}}, between the shifting you mentioned and everything we just talked through. If you could completely fix just one of these and never think about it again, which one would you choose?

(If the shifting is the only thing on the list, that’s the answer. Continue to Making It Real with it.)

